# AI Teacher Assistant — example environment file
# Copy this file to `.env` and adjust values as needed.
# NEVER put real API keys or secrets in this repository.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend (Vite). Values starting with VITE_ are embedded into the frontend
# bundle at build time.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Base URL of the FastAPI backend.
# - Leave unset for development: the Vite dev server proxies /api and /health
#   to BACKEND_HOST:BACKEND_PORT (see vite.config.ts).
# - Set it (e.g. http://127.0.0.1:8000) for packaged desktop builds so the
#   Tauri WebView talks to the backend directly.
#VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend (FastAPI). Read by backend/app/core/config.py from the project root.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where uvicorn listens for development.
#BACKEND_HOST=127.0.0.1
#BACKEND_PORT=8000

# development | production
#APP_ENVIRONMENT=development

# Comma-separated list of allowed CORS origins (the Tauri WebView origin is
# tauri://localhost on desktop builds).
#APP_CORS_ORIGINS_CSV=http://localhost:5173,http://tauri.localhost,tauri://localhost

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CrewAI. The crew is initialized WITHOUT contacting any LLM provider.
# Kickoffs happen only in later phases and require you to configure a model
# provider locally (e.g. via OPENAI_API_KEY in your own .env, never committed).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#CREW_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
